Package: hgr
Title: The hidden grammar of reserving
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R:
    person("Robin", "Van Oirbeek", , "robin.vanoirbeek@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = ""))
Description: Implements a unified framework for macro-level reserving in non-life insurance,
    based on the insight that classical reserving methods are credibility estimators.
    Includes the Negative Binomial Chain-Ladder (NB-CL) model, Unified Credibility
    Reserving (UCR), Mack's distribution-free model, classical Bühlmann-Straub
    credibility theory, model-agnostic predictive intervals via the
    Dirichlet-Multinomial parametric bootstrap, and the Compound Negative
    Binomial-Gamma (CNBG) amount-triangle model of "What Paid Triangles Identify
    about Reserve Uncertainty: Information Boundaries in Loss Reserving". UCR
    nests Chain-Ladder, Bornhuetter-Ferguson, and Cape Cod as special cases
    with data-adaptive credibility weights. The multinomial bootstrap provides
    predictive intervals for any reserving method producing development
    proportions, governed by a single Dirichlet concentration parameter c that
    doubles as a diagnostic for model adequacy. The CNBG module is a port of
    the library behind that paper's tables: the data-generating process with
    row frailty, cell shock and calendar drift, the Stage-1 quasi-Poisson mean
    structure with free or anchored levels, the two-stage second-moment
    estimator and its population target under free levels, the
    working-likelihood posterior with fourth-moment cell shapes and the
    curvature adjustment (deterministic grid or NUTS), the modular predictive
    CNBG-Mod, the WLS-cond and refit bootstraps, the kappa posterior
    diagnostic, the Fisher and Godambe information on kappa, and the exact
    frailty-augmented posterior with anchored or free levels.
    Provides functions for model fitting, prediction, variance estimation,
    parametric bootstrap, diagnostics, and model comparison.
